{"title":"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are four more girls than boys in Ms. Raub's class of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. What is the ratio of number of girls to the number of boys in her class?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/a/c9a3615f9a467e68ec7a3181dcd89d013229d1cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3 : 4\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }4 : 3\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }3 : 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }7 : 4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }2 : 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"473\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> being the number of girls in the class. The number of boys in the class is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/b/ddbf95127c944759a1d4f1ed1153350640f78533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. Since the total number of students is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73079d1b82cda1cdba2ac2bfcc4d990228c34df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g+g-4=28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />. Solving this equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20a3780b1f3f39306ab14fb58803ef2172c489d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa49ce50e3c6a4536e3eaa24090fa629b9dfbda4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16-4=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> boys in our class, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f05a9cab87404dde494a19810f1f9fd11ea676b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16:12=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~4:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"155\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To make the amount of boys and girls equal, 28 - 4 = 24.  24/2 = 12.  The girls would need to be 12 + the 4 that we subtracted = 16. The boys would be 12.  The ratio of girls to boys would be 16&#160;: 12, but simplified would be 4&#160;: 3.  Thus, the answer is 4&#160;: 3.\n</p><p>~MiracleMaths\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We should be able to divide 28 by the sum of the ratios. If we do guess and check, the only two that complete these conditions is 3:4 and 4:3 since they add up to 7. But, the number of girls has to be more than the boys, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c898aa7229f122beb192bbcf480d42f36864a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}~4:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~AhmetAcreOfLand\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/lKIgQdAOmyU\">https://youtu.be/lKIgQdAOmyU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fjbcgj5W30E\">https://youtu.be/fjbcgj5W30E</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 8\">2014 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a>